---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
    {/* Back Arrow */}
    <div class="mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center text-primary hover:text-white transition-colors">
        <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Home
      </a>
    </div>

    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <div class="mb-8">
        <img 
          src="/arclab.png" 
          alt="ARCLab Research Project" 
          class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto h-64 object-cover rounded-2xl border border-neutral/20"
        />
      </div>
      <h1 class="mb-6 font-serif text-4xl font-bold text-white">
        ARCLab Research Project: EMG-Based Prosthetic Control
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">Research Overview</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed">
          Under the Automation, Robotics and Controls Lab, currently assisting a <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7338558230274453506/" target="_blank" class="text-primary hover:text-white transition-colors underline">graduate student</a> in expanding his award-winning undergraduate capstone project focused on developing affordable prosthetic arms for Ghanaian amputees.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed mt-4">
          The project uses surface electromyography (EMG) signals and deep learning for intuitive gesture recognition and continuous control of upper-limb prostheses.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-primary">My Role & Contributions</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed">
          As an undergraduate research assistant, my role involves contributing to the AI pipeline: preprocessing EMG signals and developing lightweight neural architectures for robust gesture classification that can run efficiently on embedded systems.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral leading-relaxed mt-4">
          This research builds on work that received the Technical Excellence Award for capstone projects in mechatronics engineering at Ashesi University.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
